  "hindi": "और निश्चय ही तुम दोनों के पहले के दान हैं, जो त्रसदस्यु ने पूरुओं के लिए प्रदान किए हैं; तुम दोनों ने खेतों को जीतने वाले, उपजाऊ भूमि को जीतने वाले, दस्युओं के लिए प्रहार करने वाले, पराभव करने वाले, उग्र को दिया।",
  "english": "And indeed there are earlier gifts of you two, which Trasadasyu has bestowed for the Pūrus; you two gave a winner of fields, a winner of fertile land, a smiter for the Dasyus, overpowering, fierce.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Difficult verse. nitośe is not a form I can parse with certainty (perhaps from ni-√tuś); rendered 'has bestowed' as a guess. The object of dadathuḥ is not named in the verse. The edition prints kṣetrāsām/urvarāsām with a long vowel (compound with -sā 'winning'); split as kṣetrā-sām, urvarā-sām.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
