  "hindi": "और तुम दोनों ने पुरस्कार जीतने वाले, बहुतों को हटाने वाले, सब जातियों के दधिक्रा को दिया; सीधे उड़ने वाले, बाज़ जैसे, चितकबरे रूप वाले, तेज़, बार-बार स्तुति के योग्य, स्वामी के, वीर के समान, मनुष्यों के स्वामी को।",
  "english": "And you two gave Dadhikrā, the prize-winner, driving back many, of all peoples; straight-flying, a hawk, speckled-formed, swift, to be often extolled, of the master, like a hero, a lord of men.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Several words are uncertain: ṛjipya (rendered 'straight-flying'), pruṣita-psu ('speckled-formed'), puru-niḥ-sidhvān ('driving back many'). aryaḥ is read as genitive of arya 'master', but it could be another form; the last phrase 'nṛpatiṃ na śūram' is taken as 'like a hero, a lord of men'.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
