  "hindi": "जिसके पीछे, ढलान पर जैसे दौड़ते हुए, हर भीड़ हर्षित होकर आनन्द मनाती है; पैरों से उत्सुक, वीर के समान मेधा चाहने वाले, रथ को तेज़ चलाने वाले, वायु के समान सरकते हुए को।",
  "english": "Him who runs as if down a slope, in whom every multitude rejoices, delighted; eager with the feet, like a hero desiring wisdom, chariot-speeding, gliding like the wind.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "sīm anu is read 'along him' (sīm is an enclitic acc. particle); the construction 'yam ... dravantam ... madati' is read as 'in whom ... rejoices'. pūruḥ is read as 'multitude' (nom. sg. of pūru 'many'); a tribal name Pūru is also possible. medha-yu: medha may be 'wisdom' or 'sacrifice'; rendered 'wisdom' as in the glossary-consistent reading of 4.37.6.",
  "confidence": "low"
 },
